    {
      "text": "What interesting things have you done with science?",
      "speaker": "a",
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 2.68
    },
    {
      "text": "Oh, this one takes me back. The most interesting thing — I remember I once used a concave mirror, you know, the kind that can focus things. I used it to concentrate sunlight onto a piece of paper and tried to burn it. I did that when I was a pupil. And also, whenever I saw an interesting science video, I would retell the whole thing to my classmates, my desk mates, and they were all amazed by it.",
      "speaker": "b",
      "start": 3.15,
      "end": 25.0
    }
